    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e263">lothach</headword>
      <description>bedraggled. (Pronounced with English ‘th’ sound, i.e. ‘loth’ as in English ‘cloth’ but with the Gaelic double ‘l’ sound at the beginning of the word.)</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e272">[cramhan]</headword>
      <description>‘Tha na cramhan gos tigh’nn troimh na chracann.’</description>
    </item>
    <item><headword id="d0e280" type="heading" level="h1">4. Names for certain beasts, e.g. an animal on which the owner bestows particular attention</headword></item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e285">sùileagan</headword>
      <description>It could also mean e.g. a person who had been in very good circumstances and who, through his own foolishness, became reduced to lowly straits. Tha e ’na shùileagan a measg nan daoine.</description>
    </item>
